# GTM Profile: <Your Company>

Copy this file to `config/gtm_profile.md` and fill it in with your own
go-to-market positioning. The account-brief generator (`--brief`) feeds it to
Claude as context when it reads a scraped board-minutes document, so the brief
reflects how *you* qualify and pitch. This is your own strategy, not scraped
data - `config/gtm_profile.md` is gitignored so it never gets committed.

## Company overview
One paragraph: what you build, for whom, and your traction.

## What we sell
Your products/modules and what each does.

## Platform & security posture
Hosting, certifications, key integrations - anything that shortens a security
review or is a differentiator in certain accounts.

## Who we sell to
Primary/secondary markets, and the buyer roles that are real entry points
(vs. who merely validates).

## Problems that create a deal
The concrete trigger situations that mean a prospect needs you now.

## Positioning against the competitor set
Group competitors by category and give the one-line reframe for each.

## Signals worth scoring high
Observable events that indicate a hot account (leadership changes, audits,
budget/program moves, new programs, tech standardization, relevant open roles).

## Deprioritize or disqualify
Who to skip, and who to deprioritize unless a specific pain is present.
